FUN_0000_7c1d (the FIRST per-object UPDATE method, dispatched by c0e5, patch 243): base-lost object
pointer + absolute-host CS-table reads -> SIGSEGV on the first per-frame update (459a->c0ca->c0e5->7c1d).

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x7c1d-0x7c90; gdb crash at fist.c:20574,
param_4=0x8074xxxx garbage host addr).  c0e5 (patch 243) dispatches each object's UPDATE method with
`(int)di` (the object near-offset) as arg0 -> lands in 7c1d's param_1 (di=0xC05C observed), exactly like
d755->7bcf (patch 169/219).  But Ghidra typed 7c1d to read the object base from param_4 (a DROPPED
register = garbage) and read its two CS-relative dispatch tables at 0x7c91 / 0x7d92 as ABSOLUTE HOST
offsets.  The asm object base is DS:DI (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00), and the two tables are CS-relative (CS=0):

    7c1d: mov al,[di+0x1d]; mov [di+0xd],al ...          ; object fields, DS:DI-relative
    7c47: addb [di+0x3d],2                               ; bump state
    7c4b: mov bl,[di+0x3d]; and bx,0x1e                  ; table1 index (even, 0..0x1e)
    7c51: call *cs:0x7c91(%bx)                           ; near call word cs:[0x7c91+bx], DI live
    7c56: mov bl,[di+0x3e]; xor bh,bh                    ; table2 index (byte)
    7c5b: call *cs:0x7d92(%bx)                           ; near call word cs:[0x7d92+bx], DI live

FIX: the object host pointer = g_mem+0x1c000+di; the whole body + every callee call is already
object-relative (host-pointer correct), so re-point param_4 at it (single assignment, body untouched).
The two CS tables live in CS=0 -> read the word entry at g_mem+0x7c91+(byte[di+0x3d]&0x1e) /
g_mem+0x7d92+byte[di+0x3e], dispatched near with di (the object offset) live in arg0 (matching the
c0e5/d755 convention so a reconstructed dg+di target receives it as param_1).  Mission-cascade only
(459a is never reached by the 19 menu flows).
